---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft, FileText } from 'lucide-react';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service">
  <div class="p-6 md:p-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full space-y-6 animate-in fade-in duration-200">
    {/* Navigation header */}
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-4">
      <a href="/dashboard" class="flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-bold text-steel hover:text-primary transition">
        <ArrowLeft className="w-3.5 h-3.5" /> Back to Dashboard
      </a>
      <span class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-slate-400">Classified // Internal Use Only</span>
    </div>

    {/* Document Container */}
    <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft p-6 md:p-10 rounded-xxxl card-product-shadow space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-circle bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary">
          <FileText className="w-5 h-5" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-steel font-bold">KSP-ConAI Compliance</span>
          <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-deep">Terms of Service</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-[11px] text-stone font-medium">
        Last Updated: July 2026 | Authority: Karnataka State Police Command Centre
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-5 text-xs text-steel leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>
            By logging into the KSP-ConAI platform, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to follow these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, you must terminate your session immediately and report to your Station Administrator.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">2. Authorized Use Only</h2>
          <p>
            This portal is exclusively for the official use of personnel belonging to the Karnataka State Police. Access by any other person, or use for non-official purposes (including personal curiosity, tracking acquaintances, or unauthorized research), is strictly prohibited and constitutes a punishable offense under Section 66 of the Information Technology Act.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">3. Account Security & Responsibility</h2>
          <p>
            Officers are solely responsible for all activities conducted under their credentials. You must not share passwords, session tokens, or bypass authentication gates. If you suspect your account has been compromised, notify the IT Support Cell immediately.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">4. Prohibited Activities</h2>
          <p>
            Users are strictly forbidden from:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
            <li>Exporting raw database files, suspect graph mappings, or hotspot overlays without an authorized supervisor signature.</li>
            <li>Inputting non-police files or queries containing malicious payloads into the AI Assistant.</li>
            <li>Sharing or copying KSP-ConAI screenshots onto public networks or personal devices.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">5. Monitoring and Audit Consent</h2>
          <p>
            All network activities, database searches, and AI chatbot prompts are actively recorded, stored, and audited. KSP reserves the right to intercept, investigate, and present these session logs in administrative hearings or court proceedings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">6. Term Violations & Penalties</h2>
          <p>
            Violations of these terms will lead to immediate revocation of access permissions, disciplinary inquiry under the Karnataka Civil Services Rules, suspension, and legal prosecution under the Indian Penal Code (IPC) or relevant cybercrime laws.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-hairline-soft pt-4 flex justify-between items-center text-[10px] text-stone">
        <span>KSP-ConAI Protocol V1.0</span>
        <button onclick="window.print()" class="text-primary hover:underline font-bold cursor-pointer">Print Document</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
